    description: "DECISION REQUESTED, not a defect. Should hypergumbo-tracker and subprocess\ntests be brought into the measured coverage scope?\n\nWHAT IT WOULD BUY, measured 2026-08-14. 3,614 tests (15.9% of the suite)\nproduce no coverage rows at all: hypergumbo-tracker 2,818 (outside COV_PATHS),\nimport-time-subject 435, subprocess 255, scripts/ 106. They cost 12.4 min of\nserial time that NO trajectory can avoid, because a test coverage cannot see\ncan never be selected against -- 57% of the 21.7-min full-coverage trajectory\nis this mandatory floor. hypergumbo-tracker alone is 6.0 min of it.\n\nBringing them in would put that 6 minutes onto the board where selection can\nreach it, and would shrink the unmeasured population that Phase 3 has to\nspecial-case.\n\nWHY IT IS A DECISION AND NOT A TASK: it changes what the repo's 100%-coverage\ngate MEANS. The tracker package is currently tested in isolation with its own\nregime; subprocess coverage needs COVERAGE_PROCESS_START wiring. Both alter\nthe gate's denominator, which is an owner call, not a side effect of tuning a\nselector."  # 3b23
    fields: {}  # 3b23
- op: discuss  # d6f4
  at: '2026-11-10T21:09:43Z'  # d6f4
  by: agent  # d6f4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d6f4
  clock: 2  # d6f4
  nonce: d6f4  # d6f4
  message: "Checked 2026-11-10: what coverage bar hypergumbo-tracker is already held to. It is already 100% at every CI layer; only local smart-test and the selection index leave it out.\n\n- Per-PR (.github/workflows/ci.yml ~L830-835, ~L930): the coverage packages are derived from the changed source files (`packages/<pkg>/src`), so a PR touching packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src measures it, and `coverage report --include=<changed files> --fail-under=100` gates it like any other package.\n- Full-suite (.github/workflows/full-suite.yml ~L847-858, and the retry job ~L914): a separate tracker job runs packages/hypergumbo-tracker/tests with `--cov=packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src` and fails unless TOTAL is exactly 100% (WI-kalub \"full-suite teeth\").\n- Nightly (.github/workflows/nightly.yml ~L77, ~L170): COV_PATHS includes packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src, run with `--cov-fail-under=100`.\n- Local smart-test (scripts/smart-test ~L337): COV_PATHS lists core + the five lang packages and NOT hypergumbo-tracker. This, plus the selection index fed from it, is the only place the tracker is outside measurement.\n- packages/hypergumbo-tracker/pyproject.toml sets no fail_under of its own; the bar comes from the workflows above.\n\nSo for the TRACKER half, the decision's stated cost (\"it changes what the 100% gate means\") does not hold: the bar is already 100% in CI, and adding the tracker to smart-test's COV_PATHS holds it locally to the same bar CI already applies. What it does change: (1) local smart-test now fails on tracker coverage gaps it used to pass, which CI would have failed anyway; (2) the tracker's 2,818 tests get coverage rows, so the selection index can speak about them (the 6.0 of 12.4 min). One nuance to keep: a combined run can credit tracker lines to tests in OTHER packages; the isolated full-suite tracker job stays, so that cannot loosen the package's own bar.\n\nThe SUBPROCESS half (255 tests, plus part of scripts/' 106) is unchanged by this: COVERAGE_PROCESS_START wiring does add newly measured lines (CLI paths reached only through subprocesses) to the denominator, so that half is still the real decision.\nAgent recommendation: tracker half yes (no change to the bar); subprocess half yes, as a separate step, since it measures code no layer measures today."  # d6f4
